   *
   * This operation immediately terminates the specified timer without creating a timelog entry. The timer must belong to the authenticated employee making the request. Once discarded, the timer is permanently removed and cannot be recovered.
   *
   * The employee must have an active timer to discard. If the timer does not exist or belongs to another employee, the system returns a not found error. This operation does not generate any activity log entry since discarded timers do not create historical records.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param timerId Unique identifier of the timer to discard
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor member
   * @x-autobe-specification Validate that the timer exists in the database. Verify the timer belongs to the authenticated employee by matching erp_hrm_employee_id with the current session's employee record. If the timer does not exist, return 404 not found error. If the timer belongs to another employee, return 404 not found error (do not reveal existence of other employees' timers for privacy). Permanently delete the timer record from erp_hrm_timers table using cascade delete. Do not create any timelog entry. Do not create any activity log entry. Return 204 No Content on success.
